.IX Title "Lucy::Store::Folder 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Store::Folder 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Store::Folder \- Abstract class representing a directory.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\&    # Abstract base class.
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
A “file” within a Folder might be a real file on disk – or it might be a
RAM buffer.  Similarly, \fBDelete()\fR might delete a file from the file system, or
a key-value pair from a hash, or something else.
.PP
The archetypal implementation of Folder,
FSFolder, represents a directory on
the file system holding a collection of files.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Store::Folder isa Clownfish::Obj.
